message: "If you use PrivCord in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "PrivCord: private, end-to-end encrypted, peer-to-peer messenger with no account or phone number"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "anandkrishna1900"
repository-code: "https://github.com/raiden6767/PrivCord"
license-url: "https://github.com/raiden6767/PrivCord/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - encrypted messenger
  - end-to-end encryption
  - peer-to-peer
  - private messaging
  - no phone number
  - WebRTC
  - Bluetooth mesh
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - Rust
  - Android
  - Windows
abstract: >-
  PrivCord is a private messenger for Windows and Android. Chats are end-to-end encrypted and travel directly between
  devices over WebRTC or Bluetooth, with no account, phone number or server that can read them. It supports groups,
  files, public channels, an offline Bluetooth mesh, and multi-device sync, on a shared Rust engine.
